<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virarajendra Chola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1063–1070</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virarajendra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> was a king of the Chola dynasty of south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, ruling from 1063 to 1070, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-chola-i">Rajendra Chola I</a>. He fought repeated wars against the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a>, defeating them at Kudal Sangamam, and campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>. His inscriptions record a naval expedition about 1068 that conquered Kadaram (Kedah) and restored its ruler, who had sought Chola help.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virarajendra-chola.jpg" alt="Virarajendra Chola" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Virarajendra_Chola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
